{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-36110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-25{z}^{2}+16x+50z+91 & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}+4x)+{y}^{2}-25({z}^{2}-2z)+91 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x+2)^{2}-4]+{y}^{2}-25[(z-1)^{2}-1]+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}-16+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+25+91 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-25(z-1)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-36110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "faa633709c3c07cf19ab142216dd2ca65f1626fe983dbabc91e20946840b6062"} {"question" "q-36110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-36110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(-2,0,1)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(2,0,-1)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(1,0,5)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-36110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-2,0,1)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand an ellipsoid centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an ellipsoid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-2,0),\\,a=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{7},\\,c=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "faa633709c3c07cf19ab142216dd2ca65f1626fe983dbabc91e20946840b6062"} {"question" "q-164403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A cylinder"] ["text" "A hyperboloid"] ["text" "A paraboloid"] ["text" "A sphere"] ["text" "An ellipsoid"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An ellipsoid"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $a=b=1,\\,c=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "faa633709c3c07cf19ab142216dd2ca65f1626fe983dbabc91e20946840b6062"} {"question" "q-164508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=c=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "faa633709c3c07cf19ab142216dd2ca65f1626fe983dbabc91e20946840b6062"} {"question" "q-164516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface ${y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-4y)-({z}^{2}+6z)-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4-(z+3)^{2}+9-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2} & =x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "faa633709c3c07cf19ab142216dd2ca65f1626fe983dbabc91e20946840b6062"} {"question" "q-164549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067670/state.json" "file_sha256" "17e6a361294fe8f36e53066153c94a80092e9588b310b52d5e81fec936bd9b21"} {"question" "q-164549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(-1,2,3)$"] ["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,-2,3)$"] ["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3)$"] ["text" "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,2,-3)$"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Devel